1. Set up your development environment:

You can use the Chrome Web Store to create a new Chrome extension. Make sure you have the necessary Chrome extensions enabled in your browser.

2. Create a new extension project:

Navigate to the Chrome Web Store and search for "Extension Builder". Click on the Extension Builder Extension file and then select "Create Extension" to create your extension project.

3. Define the extension's manifest:

The manifest file is a JSON file that contains information about your extension, such as its name, permissions, and description. You can create a new JSON file in the root directory of your extension project to define the extension's information.

Here is an example manifest file:

```json
{
  "manifest_version": 2,
  "name": "Your_Extension_Name",
  "version": "1.0",
  "description": "Your extension description",
  "permissions": [
    {
      "name": "storage",
      "scope": [
        "storage"
      ],
      "permissions": [
        "storage"
      ],
      "grant_files": ["https://www.example.com/storage.html"]
    },
    {
      "name": "active_directory_access",
      "scope": ["profile", "email"],
      "permissions": [
        "storage",
        "open_emails"
      ],
      "grant_files": ["https://www.example.com/storage.html"]
    }
  ],
  "background": {
    "scripts": [
      {
        "src": "extension-background.js",
        "type": "text/javascript"
      }
    ]
  },
  "background_policy": {
    "match_existing_policy": "background"
  },
  "background_policy_override": {
    "match_existing_policy": "background"
  }
}
```

